// N108: QSA prefill block selection on Intel Xe2 (Arc Pro B70): fused indexer scores + exact radix top-k per row,
// torch.ops.n108qsa.prefill_scores / prefill_select. Drop-in for SGLang torch_qsa_mqa_prefill + exl3xpu qsa_fast_topk:
//   logits[r, n] = sum_h relu(q[r, h] . k[n]) / score_div      (fp32 dots of bf16 values; score_div = sqrt(D))
//   for n in [row_starts[r], row_ends[r]); top-k by value, ties at the threshold -> lowest index (Strata's rule);
//   output: selected block indices relative to row_starts[r] in ascending order, then -1 (valid-first layout).
//
// Structure ported from Strata (github.com/Niko1221/Strata, MIT; sycl/src/kernels/cuda/qsa_select.dp.cpp:
// block_scores_kernel and block_topk_reg_kernel / qsa_block_topk), adapted to this server's indexer (4 heads x 128,
// bf16 q and compressed keys, plain relu-sum logits, no tail-block bonus, block-count budget):
//   * scores: lane-per-block (the key of one compressed block per lane, held as packed bf16 in registers), q of a
//     few rows in SLM, broadcast lane by lane; a work-group covers 256 blocks x RPW rows;
//   * top-k: one work-group per row, 8-bit radix passes over the orderable keys (histograms in SLM), then the exact
//     selection > threshold plus the first (lowest-index) ties, positions from a work-group exclusive scan.
//
